join guard left
if {cook_introduced} == false:
	set {cook_introduced} = true
	join detective right
	detective: Tell me about yourself.
	guard: I'm a guard.
	guard: ...
	detective: ...
	guard: ...
	guard: Fine.
	guard: I've been doing this a while. I tend to bounce around between estates. Keeps the monotony from getting to my head.
	guard: At least I'm not stuck here long term like those other guys.
	guard: Been a while since the last time I guarded for a vampire's event. They're weird folk aren't they.
	detective: What can you tell me about the events of the murder?
	guard: Not much, to be honest.
	guard: I remained outside the whole time, as a guard is meant to.
	guard: I was brought inside at one point to address an argument that had started between [COOK] and one of the other vampire guests, [FRIEND] I think it was.
	guard: [FRIEND] was trying to blame [COOK] for Dracula collapsing.
	guard (angry): I wish I could have helped [COOK], but I honestly wasn't sure what to say.
	guard (speaking): The other vampire, [NIECE], seemed pretty tired of it too, so I decided we should both head upstairs to check on Dracula.
	guard: That's when we found him dead in his bedroom.
	guard: Honestly, though, I'd be careful about [NIECE]. The look on her face made me feel almost like she wasn't surprised, like she had already known he was dead.
guard: ...
- Present evidence
